# Git-Flow Branching

Use [git-flow](https://nvie.com/posts/a-successful-git-branching-model/) for all ticket work.

## Permanent Branches

- `main` — production-ready code only
- `develop` — integration branch for the next release

## Branch Types

| Type | Branch from | Merge into | Use for |
|------|-------------|------------|---------|
| `feature/` | `develop` | `develop` | New work, enhancements |
| `bugfix/` | `develop` | `develop` | Non-urgent fixes |
| `release/` | `develop` | `main` + `develop` | Release prep |
| `hotfix/` | `main` | `main` + `develop` | Urgent production fixes |

## Opening a Ticket

1. Update the base branch: `git checkout develop && git pull`
2. Create a branch named after the ticket:
   - `feature/<ticket-id>-<short-description>` — new work
   - `bugfix/<ticket-id>-<short-description>` — fixes
   - `hotfix/<ticket-id>-<short-description>` — urgent production fixes (branch from `main`)
3. Do all ticket work on that branch; never commit directly to `main` or `develop`

```bash
# Example: opening ticket ANSI-42
git checkout develop && git pull
git checkout -b feature/ANSI-42-add-color-palette
```

## Closing a Ticket

1. Push the branch and open a PR targeting the correct base:
   - `feature/` and `bugfix/` → `develop`
   - `hotfix/` → `main` (then back-merge to `develop`)
2. **Merge the PR automatically** — do not leave feature PRs open waiting for manual merge. After the PR is created and checks pass (or immediately if there are no required checks), merge it:
   ```bash
   gh pr merge --squash --delete-branch
   ```
   Use `--merge` instead of `--squash` only if the repo convention requires a merge commit. Never force-merge if checks are failing; fix or report the blocker first.
3. Sync local `develop` (or `main` for hotfixes) and delete the local feature branch
4. Move the Linear ticket to **Done** only after the PR is merged

```bash
# Example: ship a feature ticket end-to-end
git push -u origin HEAD
gh pr create --base develop --title "..." --body "..."
gh pr merge --squash --delete-branch
git checkout develop && git pull
git branch -d feature/ANSI-42-add-color-palette
```

## Release Flow

1. `git checkout -b release/x.y.z develop`
2. Bump version, fix release-only issues, tag on `main` after merge
3. Merge `release/x.y.z` into both `main` and `develop`

## Rules

- Never force-push `main` or `develop`
- Keep branch names lowercase with hyphens; include ticket ID when available
- One ticket = one branch; do not mix unrelated work
